{#
============================================================================
WH40K Cheat Sheet — Jinja2 / WeasyPrint template
Modeled on wh40k_11e_cheat_sheet_v1.pdf (11th edition, 3-page, 2-column).

Rendered by the feature-002 pipeline (Jinja2 -> HTML -> WeasyPrint -> PDF).
This is a COMPLETE HTML document with print CSS (@page), ready for WeasyPrint.
Autoescape is ON: plain-text fields are escaped; fields ending in `_html`
are trusted, pre-authored HTML fragments injected via `| safe`.

The WH40K logo (images/logo_40k.png) appears as a large, faint (5% opacity),
45-degree-rotated background watermark behind every page's content, via the
fixed, unconditional `.page-watermark` <img> below — it is NOT an authored
content-block flag, it always renders regardless of document.blocks content.
DOM order (placed before the document's own content) keeps it painting behind
everything; do not add z-index, which was found to hide it entirely (see
feature-010's research.md). The pipeline verifies the logo file exists before
rendering (fails loudly if missing, per feature-010) since WeasyPrint itself
does not.

document.print_friendly (bool, default false) — pipeline-set only, never an
authored content.yaml field (feature-011). When true: every :root color custom
property resolves to its grayscale equivalent (computed server-side, since
@page margin-box content inherits from the page context, not from <body> —
a body-scoped override would not reach the running header/footer), and the
watermark <img> above is omitted entirely (not merely hidden) via the Jinja
conditional around it.

EXPECTED CONTEXT (all optional-safe; missing keys degrade gracefully):

document:
title: "Warhammer 40,000 — 11th Edition Cheat Sheet" # running header
subtitle: "Quick reference" # optional
edition: "11e"
revision: "2026-08-01-00" # shown in footer
language: "en"
blocks: [ <block>, ... ] # ordered; flow across 2 balanced columns,
  # split into separate pages at page_break markers,
  # or realigned to a left column (same page if
  # room remains) at column_reset markers

  <block> types (see full reference at bottom of this comment):
    phase | spanning_headline | subsection | paragraph | list | callout | table |
    keyvals | glossary | stratagem | page_break | column_reset

    { type: "phase", title: "1. COMMAND PHASE" }
    { type: "spanning_headline", title: "NEW MAJOR SECTION" } # like phase, but its
    # text and background span the full width of
    # BOTH columns, providing a clear-cut visual
    # break; visually distinguished from `phase`
    # purely by its width (same color/typography)
    { type: "subsection", title: "Battle-Shock" }
    { type: "paragraph", text: "..." | html: "<b>..</b>" }
    { type: "list", single_column: true|false, # optional, default false; when true
    # the list spans the full width of both
    # columns instead of being confined to one
    items: [ "text", {text:"..", sub:["..", ..]}, .. ] }
    { type: "callout", text: "..", variant: "warn"|"info" }
    { type: "table", columns: ["S vs T","Need"], rows: [["S >= 2xT","2+"], ..] }
    { type: "keyvals", title:"Attack Sequence",
    items:[ {label:"1. Hit Roll", text:".."}, .. ] }
    { type: "glossary", title:"CORE ABILITIES",
    spanning: true|false, # optional, default false; when true
    # the title bar spans both columns like
    # spanning_headline (terms list unaffected)
    terms:[ {term:"ASSAULT", text:".."}, .. ] }
    { type: "stratagem", title:"COMMAND RE-ROLL", cost:"1CP",
    timing:"either"|"your"|"opponent",
    when:"..", target:"..", effect:"..", restrictions:".." }
    { type: "page_break" } # forces everything after it onto a new page; no other
    # fields; leading/trailing/consecutive markers never
    # produce a blank page (empty segments are dropped)
    { type: "column_reset" } # realigns everything after it to a left column; forces
    # a new page only if no room remains on the current one;
    # no other fields. Adjacent to a page_break with nothing
    # between them, page_break always wins (forces the page).

    Rich-markup convention: a single-text block/item may replace `text` with
    `html` (paragraph, callout, list item, keyval, glossary term). A multi-field
    block (stratagem) replaces field `X` with `X_html`. `html`/`*_html` values are
    injected via `| safe`; everything else is autoescaped.
    ============================================================================
    #}
    {%- macro render_list(items) -%}
    <ul>
      {%- for it in items -%}
      {%- if it is mapping -%}
      <li>{{ (it.html | safe) if it.html is defined else it.text }}
        {%- if it.sub is defined and it.sub -%}
        <ul class="sub">
          {%- for s in it.sub -%}
          <li>{{ (s.html | safe) if (s is mapping and s.html is defined) else (s.text if s is mapping else s) }}</li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
        {%- endif -%}
      </li>
      {%- else -%}
      <li>{{ it }}</li>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
    {%- endmacro -%}
    {%- macro render_block(block, i18n) -%}
    {%- set t = block.type | default('paragraph') -%}

    {%- if t == 'phase' -%}
    <h2 class="phase">{{ block.title }}</h2>

    {%- elif t == 'spanning_headline' -%}
    <h2 class="phase phase--spanning">{{ block.title }}</h2>

    {%- elif t == 'subsection' -%}
    <h3 class="subsection">{{ block.title }}</h3>

    {%- elif t == 'paragraph' -%}
    <p class="body">{{ (block.html | safe) if block.html is defined else block.text }}</p>

    {%- elif t == 'list' -%}
    <div class="block{{ ' block--full-width' if block.single_column | default(false) else '' }}">{{
      render_list(block['items'] | default([])) }}</div>

    {%- elif t == 'callout' -%}
    {%- set variant = block.variant | default('warn') -%}
    <div class="callout callout--{{ variant }}">
      <span class="callout__icon">{{ '⚠' if variant == 'warn' else 'ℹ' }}</span>
      <span class="callout__text">{{ (block.html | safe) if block.html is defined else block.text }}</span>
    </div>

    {%- elif t == 'table' -%}
    <table class="data">
      {%- if block.columns is defined -%}
      <thead>
        <tr>{% for c in block.columns %}<th>{{ c }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
      </thead>
      {%- endif -%}
      <tbody>
        {%- for row in block['rows'] | default([]) -%}
        <tr>{% for cell in row %}<td>{{ cell }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    {%- elif t == 'keyvals' -%}
    <div class="block keyvals">
      {%- if block.title is defined %}<h4 class="minor">{{ block.title }}</h4>{% endif -%}
      <dl>
        {%- for kv in block['items'] | default([]) -%}
        <dt>{{ kv.label }}</dt>
        <dd>{{ (kv.html | safe) if kv.html is defined else kv.text }}</dd>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </dl>
    </div>

    {%- elif t == 'glossary' -%}
    <h2 class="phase{{ ' phase--spanning' if block.spanning | default(false) else '' }}">{{ block.title | default('Core
      Abilities') }}</h2>
    <div class="glossary{{ ' glossary--spanning' if block.spanning | default(false) else '' }}">
      {%- for g in block['terms'] | default([]) -%}
      <p class="term"><span class="term__name">{{ g.term }}:</span> {{ (g.html | safe) if g.html is defined else g.text
        }}</p>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- elif t == 'stratagem' -%}
    {%- set timing = block.timing | default('either') -%}
    <section class="stratagem">
      <header class="stratagem__head">
        <span class="stratagem__title">{{ block.title }}</span>
        {%- if block.cost is defined %}<span class="stratagem__cost">{{ block.cost }}</span>{% endif -%}
      </header>
      <div class="stratagem__timing stratagem__timing--{{ timing }}">
        {%- if timing == 'your' -%}▶ {{ i18n.timing_your | default('YOUR TURN') }}
        {%- elif timing == 'opponent' -%}◀ {{ i18n.timing_opponent | default("OPPONENT'S TURN") }}
        {%- else -%}◆ {{ i18n.timing_either | default("EITHER PLAYER'S TURN") }}{%- endif -%}
      </div>
      <div class="stratagem__body">
        {%- if block.when is defined or block.when_html is defined %}<p><span class="lbl">WHEN:</span> {{
          (block.when_html | safe) if block.when_html is defined else block.when }}</p>{% endif -%}
        {%- if block.target is defined or block.target_html is defined %}<p><span class="lbl">TARGET:</span> {{
          (block.target_html | safe) if block.target_html is defined else block.target }}</p>{% endif -%}
        {%- if block.effect is defined or block.effect_html is defined %}<p><span class="lbl">EFFECT:</span> {{
          (block.effect_html | safe) if block.effect_html is defined else block.effect }}</p>{% endif -%}
        {%- if block.restrictions is defined or block.restrictions_html is defined %}<p><span
            class="lbl">RESTRICTIONS:</span> {{ (block.restrictions_html | safe) if block.restrictions_html is defined
          else block.restrictions }}</p>{% endif -%}
      </div>
    </section>

    {%- else -%}
    <p class="body">{{ (block.html | safe) if block.html is defined else block.text }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- endmacro -%}
    {%- set i18n = document.i18n if (document is defined and document.i18n is defined) else {} -%}
    {%- set print_friendly = document.print_friendly | default(false) if document is defined else false -%}
    <!doctype html>
    <html lang="{{ document.language | default('en') }}">

    <head>
      <meta charset="utf-8">
      <title>{{ document.title | default('Warhammer 40,000 Cheat Sheet') }}</title>
      <style>
        {#- print-friendly mode (feature-011): every custom property below is a grayscale
     equivalent when print_friendly is set. Resolved here at :root (rather than a
     body-scoped override) because @page margin-box content (the running header/footer)
     inherits custom properties from the page context, not from <body> — a class-based
     override on <body> would not reach var(--green-dark)/var(--muted) inside @top-center
     /@bottom-left/@bottom-right below. Distinct grey shades per stratagem-timing and
     callout variant preserve their non-color distinguishability (icon/text labels
     already do most of that work; see data-model.md §2/§5). #}
        :root {
          --green-dark: {{ '#262626' if print_friendly else '#1e4d34' }};
          /* phase header bars */
          --green-sub: {{ '#595959' if print_friendly else '#5f8a6e' }};
          /* subsection bars   */
          --green-line: {{ '#333333' if print_friendly else '#24513a' }};
          --ink: {{ '#111111' if print_friendly else '#17170f' }};
          --muted: {{ '#444444' if print_friendly else '#444' }};
          --cream: {{ '#f2f2f2' if print_friendly else '#f6f1d8' }};
          /* callout bg        */
          --cream-brd: {{ '#999999' if print_friendly else '#cdbf7a' }};
          --info-bg: {{ '#e0e0e0' if print_friendly else '#e6eef6' }};
          --info-brd: {{ '#888888' if print_friendly else '#a9c3dc' }};
          --your-bg: {{ '#ffffff' if print_friendly else '#dcefe1' }};
          --your-ink: {{ '#000000' if print_friendly else '#1f6b3d' }};
          /* ▶ your turn      */
          --opp-bg: {{ '#cccccc' if print_friendly else '#f7e0e0' }};
          --opp-ink: {{ '#000000' if print_friendly else '#9c3030' }};
          /* ◀ opponent turn  */
          --either-bg: {{ '#e6e6e6' if print_friendly else '#f6ecc8' }};
          --either-ink: {{ '#000000' if print_friendly else '#8a6d16' }};
          /* ◆ either         */
          --rule: {{ '#999999' if print_friendly else '#b9bfb0' }};
        }

        @page {
          size: A4 portrait;
          margin: 7mm 6mm 8mm 6mm;

          @top-center {
            content: "{{ document.title | default('Warhammer 40,000 — Cheat Sheet') }}";
            font: 700 7pt/1 "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif;
            color: var(--green-dark);
          }

          @bottom-left {
            content: "{% if document.edition is defined %}Edition {{ document.edition }}{% endif %}{% if document.revision is defined %} · rev {{ document.revision }}{% endif %}";
            font: 6.5pt/1 "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif;
            color: var(--muted);
          }

          @bottom-right {
            content: "{{ i18n.page | default('Page') }} " counter(page) " / " counter(pages);
            font: 6.5pt/1 "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif;
            color: var(--muted);
          }
        }

        * {
          box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        html {
          font-family: "DejaVu Sans", "Noto Sans", sans-serif;
        }

        body {
          margin: 0;
          color: var(--ink);
          font-size: 7.55pt;
          line-height: 1.2;
        }

        /* full-page diagonal watermark, repeats on every page via position:fixed; sized so
     the rotated bounding box (a square, side = (w+h)*cos45deg) fits entirely within
     the page without cropping (page width is the binding constraint for A4 portrait);
     left/top account for position:fixed's containing block being the content box, not
     the physical page edge (verified empirically). No z-index: DOM order alone (placed
     before the document's own content) is what keeps it behind everything — a negative
     z-index was tried and hides the watermark entirely (pushes it behind the page's own
     background), so deliberately omitted. */
        .page-watermark {
          position: fixed;
          left: -14.71mm;
          top: 106.72mm;
          width: 227.42mm;
          height: 69.56mm;
          transform: rotate(45deg);
          opacity: 0.05;
        }

        /* two balanced columns, like the source sheet */
        .sheet {
          column-count: 2;
          column-gap: 5mm;
        }

        .sheet+.sheet {
          break-before: page;
        }

        .sheet+.sheet.sheet--soft {
          break-before: auto;
        }

        .sheet>* {
          break-inside: avoid;
        }

        /* --- headers --- */
        h2.phase {
          break-inside: avoid;
          break-after: avoid;
          margin: 4.5pt 0 2pt;
          padding: 1.7pt 5pt;
          background: var(--green-dark);
          color: #fff;
          font-size: 8.2pt;
          font-weight: 700;
          text-transform: uppercase;
          letter-spacing: .3px;
        }

        .sheet>h2.phase:first-child {
          margin-top: 0;
        }

        h2.phase--spanning {
          column-span: all;
          margin-top: 1em;
        }

        h3.subsection {
          break-inside: avoid;
          break-after: avoid;
          margin: 3pt 0 1.6pt;
          padding: 1.3pt 5pt;
          background: var(--green-sub);
          color: #fff;
          font-size: 7.5pt;
          font-weight: 700;
        }

        h4.minor {
          margin: 2.5pt 0 1.2pt;
          font-size: 7.5pt;
          font-weight: 700;
          color: var(--green-dark);
        }

        /* --- body text & lists --- */
        p.body {
          margin: 1.4pt 0;
        }

        .block {
          margin: 1.4pt 0;
        }

        .block--full-width {
          column-span: all;
        }

        ul {
          margin: 1.4pt 0 1.4pt;
          padding-left: 10pt;
        }

        ul li {
          margin: .6pt 0;
        }

        ul.sub {
          list-style: none;
          padding-left: 8pt;
          margin: 1pt 0;
        }

        ul.sub>li {
          position: relative;
          padding-left: 8pt;
        }

        ul.sub>li::before {
          content: "–";
          position: absolute;
          left: 0;
          color: var(--muted);
        }

        b,
        strong {
          font-weight: 700;
        }

        /* --- callout / warning box --- */
        .callout {
          break-inside: avoid;
          display: flex;
          gap: 3pt;
          align-items: flex-start;
          margin: 2pt 0;
          padding: 2.2pt 4pt;
          background: var(--cream);
          border: .6pt solid var(--cream-brd);
          border-radius: 2pt;
          font-size: 7.2pt;
        }

        .callout--info {
          background: var(--info-bg);
          border-color: var(--info-brd);
        }

        .callout__icon {
          color: var(--either-ink);
          font-weight: 700;
        }

        .callout--info .callout__icon {
          color: #2f6ba3;
        }

        /* --- data table (e.g. wound roll S vs T) --- */
        table.data {
          break-inside: avoid;
          width: 100%;
          border-collapse: collapse;
          margin: 2pt 0;
          font-size: 7.3pt;
        }

        table.data th {
          background: var(--green-dark);
          color: #fff;
          text-align: left;
          padding: 1.3pt 4pt;
          font-weight: 700;
        }

        table.data td {
          padding: 1.1pt 4pt;
          border: .5pt solid var(--rule);
        }

        table.data tbody tr:nth-child(even) td {
          background: #f2f4ef;
        }

        /* --- key/value sequence (e.g. Attack Sequence) --- */
        .keyvals dl {
          margin: 2pt 0;
        }

        .keyvals dt {
          font-weight: 700;
          margin-top: 1.5pt;
        }

        .keyvals dd {
          margin: 0 0 1pt 0;
        }

        /* --- glossary (Core Abilities) --- */
        .glossary {
          column-count: 2;
          column-gap: 5mm;
          font-size: 7.1pt;
        }

        .glossary--spanning {
          column-span: all;
        }

        .glossary .term {
          margin: 1.1pt 0;
          break-inside: avoid;
        }

        .glossary .term__name {
          font-weight: 700;
        }

        /* --- stratagem cards --- */
        .stratagem {
          break-inside: avoid;
          margin: 3pt 0;
          border: .7pt solid var(--green-dark);
          border-radius: 2.5pt;
          overflow: hidden;
        }

        .stratagem__head {
          display: flex;
          justify-content: space-between;
          align-items: center;
          background: var(--green-dark);
          color: #fff;
          padding: 1.9pt 5pt;
        }

        .stratagem__title {
          font-weight: 700;
          font-size: 7.7pt;
          text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        .stratagem__cost {
          font-weight: 700;
          font-size: 7.6pt;
          background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .18);
          padding: .5pt 4pt;
          border-radius: 6pt;
        }

        .stratagem__timing {
          font-weight: 700;
          font-size: 6.6pt;
          letter-spacing: .3px;
          padding: 1.3pt 5pt;
          border-bottom: .5pt solid var(--rule);
        }

        .stratagem__timing--your {
          background: var(--your-bg);
          color: var(--your-ink);
        }

        .stratagem__timing--opponent {
          background: var(--opp-bg);
          color: var(--opp-ink);
        }

        .stratagem__timing--either {
          background: var(--either-bg);
          color: var(--either-ink);
        }

        .stratagem__body {
          padding: 2.2pt 5pt;
        }

        .stratagem__body p {
          margin: 1.1pt 0;
        }

        .stratagem__body .lbl {
          font-weight: 700;
          color: var(--green-dark);
        }

        {%- if print_friendly %}
        /* the two hard-coded (non-custom-property) colors in this stylesheet also need a
     grayscale equivalent when print-friendly; placed last so equal-specificity cascade
     order lets these win over the rules above they override; both live in normal body
     content (not a @page margin box), so this override is safe here. */
        .callout--info .callout__icon {
          color: #333333;
        }

        table.data tbody tr:nth-child(even) td {
          background: #f0f0f0;
        }
        {%- endif %}
      </style>
    </head>

    <body class="{{ 'print-friendly' if print_friendly else '' }}">
      {%- if not print_friendly %}
      <img class="page-watermark" src="../images/logo_40k.png" alt="">
      {%- endif %}
      <article class="cheatsheet">
        {%- for segment in group_by_breaks(document.blocks if document is defined and document.blocks is defined else
        []) %}
        <div class="sheet{{ ' sheet--soft' if segment.break_type == 'soft' else '' }}">
          {%- for block in segment.blocks -%}
          {{ render_block(block, i18n) }}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </article>
    </body>

    </html>